      "message": "\u003e Eventually (very soon) all the users will need to be updated and `SkXPSDocument.cpp` will not depend on either. Even as things are the Bazel build could work by just always setting `SK_DISABLE_LEGACY_XPS_FACTORIES`.\n\u003e \n\u003e Also, need to add these (in their own targets) in `include/docs/BUILD.bazel` and `bazel/exporter_tool/main.go` updated to export them into `gn/xps.gni` (run `make -C bazel generate_gni` or equivalent as described in `bazel/exporter_tool/README.md`.\n\nOoops... I was working on the CL on Windows, but then switched to Linux to work on the Bazel/gni stuff.  It turned out that I uploaded a separate CL from Linux, rather than uploading a new patchset (I\u0027ve incorrectly thought that I don\u0027t need to to `git cl issue \u003cnumber\u003e` after a direct `git checkout` of the commits from Gerrit).\n\nDone.\n\n\u003e Should also update `XPSSink::draw` in `DMSrcSkink.cpp` to call the new `SkXPS::MakeDocument`. See `PDFSink::draw` for the equivalent there. May need to update the build of the `skia` target in `BUILD.gn` to depend on one of the new `xps_libpng_helpers` or `xps_rustpng_helpers` like the existing dependency on `pdf_jpeg_helpers`.\n\nAck.  I\u0027ll work on that on the Windows machine (where I can more easily confirm that everything still builds).\n\nLeaving this comment unresolved - I am still working on that part.",
